
                                                    MERGE COMMAND


Performs Merging of 2 or more hex file.

Below is the syntax :
          merge  merge -count [count of no. of files to be merged] -file [file1 name] -fileType [file one type] -file [file two name] -fileType [file two type] -igcks true write -out output.hex

------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SWITCHES          |    DESCRIPTION																	
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-count			  | Count of total number of file to be merged. By default it is 1.	 				
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-file			  | Hex file name.												 					
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-filetype		  | Hex file type.												 					
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-overwrite	      | Set overwrite either with true or false. By default it is false.   				
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-mode		      | Boolean attribute that specifies the Endianness. By default it is true. 		
			      | True -> little endian															
			      | False -> big endian	Not mandatory												
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-igcks	   	      | Boolean attribute to ignore line checksum. By default it is false				
------------------+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example:

	1)	merge -count 2 -file CB.hex -fileType hex -file CB17.hex -fileType hex -igcks true write -out output.hex

		
